      "id": "harmonic-hardy-classes-and-fatou-boundary-limits-examples",
      "location": "Final paragraph",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The page says the Poisson extension remains bounded below “along a tangential curve approaching 1.” The cited counterexample establishes u(z_n) ≥ (π+1)⁻² at discrete points z_n and that their approach is tangential; it gives no continuous curve or lower bound between those points. The sequence witness does not license the stronger curve claim.",
