      "id": "lem-circle-maximal-weak-one-one",
      "location": "Step 4.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 4.1 defines Î_i = {η : d(c_i,η) < 3h_i} and says it “is T when 3h_i ≥ 1/2.” At equality, the antipode has distance exactly 1/2 and is excluded, so Î_i is T minus that point. Its measure is still 1, and the later estimate remains valid.",
